"Phase 1 of M Oscar fully taken-up at launch (https://theedgemalaysia.com/article/phase-1-m-oscar-fully-takenup-launch)\nciteturn291search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; KUALA LUMPUR (Oct 8): Some 200 units from Phase 1 of M Oscar, Mah Sing Group Bhd’s new high-rise residential project were fully sold out over its launch weekend on Oct 5 and 6. ... Built-up sizes of the units range from 708 sq ft to 1,198 sq ft and are priced from RM428,000.\n\nKUALA LUMPUR (Oct 8): Some 200 units from Phase 1 of M Oscar, Mah Sing Group Bhd’s new high-rise residential project were fully sold out over its launch weekend on Oct 5 and 6.\n\nThe development located off Kuchai Lama comprises four unit types: 2 bedrooms, 3 bedrooms, 4 bedrooms and dual-key layouts. Built-up sizes of the units range from 708 sq ft to 1,198 sq ft and are priced from RM428,000.\n\n“We are heartened by the feedback from customers who liked what they saw in the show units as we have put a lot of thought into the design and practical layout.\n\n“They also liked the project’s concept elements, for example the grand lobby, 35 features and facilities, and very importantly, the strategic location,” said Mah Sing director of group strategy and operations Lionel Leong in a press release today.\n\nFollowing the success of phase 1, the developer will be launching another 200 units with an early bird rebate of 2%.\n\nM Oscar is strategically located off Kuchai Lama within the vicinity of mature neighbourhoods of Happy Garden, Sri Petaling and Bukit Jalil.\n\nIt lies about 9km away from Mid Valley City and 13km from Kuala Lumpur city centre.\n\nIt is also highly accessible via various expressways such as the New Pantai Expressway (NPE), Silk Highways, Maju Expressway and KESAS.\n\nIn terms of public transportation, M Oscar is located some 800m from the upcoming Taman Naga Emas MRT2 station where shuttle services will be provided.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFirst 200 units of M Oscar fully sold (https://theedgemalaysia.com/article/first-200-units-m-oscar-fully-sold)\nciteturn291search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.0 years ago; Crawled: last week; This article first appeared in City & Country, The Edge Malaysia Weekly on October 14, 2019 - October 20, 2019The first 200 units of South Tower (Phase 1) of Mah Sing Group Bhd’s M Oscar were fully taken up during their launch on the weekend of Oct 5 and 6.The remaining 232 units of the tower were released for sale on Oct 8 with an early bird rebate of 2%. ... Due for completion in September 2023, the towers offer two to four-bedroom layouts with built-ups ranging from 708 to 1,198 sq ft.\n\nThis article first appeared in City & Country, The Edge Malaysia Weekly on October 14, 2019 - October 20, 2019\n\nThe first 200 units of South Tower (Phase 1) of Mah Sing Group Bhd’s M Oscar were fully taken up during their launch on the weekend of Oct 5 and 6. The remaining 232 units of the tower were released for sale on Oct 8 with an early bird rebate of 2%.\n\nNorth Tower, with a total of 478 units, will be open for sale later, depending on market conditions.\n\nBuilt on a 4.63-acre freehold parcel off Jalan Kuchai Lama in Kuala Lumpur, M Oscar will comprise two blocks with a total of 910 serviced apartments and have a gross development value of RM500 million.\n\nDue for completion in September 2023, the towers offer two to four-bedroom layouts with built-ups ranging from 708 to 1,198 sq ft. The largest units, with a built-up of 1,198 sq ft, are dual-key. Selling prices start at RM428,000.\n\n“We are heartened the feedback from homebuyers who liked our show units as we put in effort to create modern designs and practical layouts,” said group director of strategy and operations Lionel Leong in an Oct 8 press release.\n\n“The target market are mainly first-time homebuyers, singletons, young families and investors. They [buyers] liked the concept elements, such as the grand loband facilities, and the strategic location,” Leong added.\n\nThe project features a 2.7-acre facility podium offering, among others, a swimming pool, children’s playground, gymnasium, Jacuzzi and multipurpose hall. The maintenance fee is 35 sen psf.\n\nNearamenities include NSK Trade City, The Store, Mid Valley Megamall, Nu Sentral, SJK(C) La Salle, SMK Sri Sentosa, Institut Latihan Perindustrian Kuala Lumpur and International Medical University.\n\nThe Taman Naga Emas MRT station is under construction 800m from the project. The mass rapid transit station is part of MRT Line 2, which is due to be operational in 2022.\n\nThe project is easily accessible via New Pantai Expressway (NPE), Maju Expressway, Shah Alam Expressway, Kuala Lumpur-Seremban Expressway and Federal Highway.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMah Sing’s M Oscar coming up off Kuchai Lama (https://theedgemalaysia.com/article/mah-sings-m-oscar-coming-kuchai-lama)\nciteturn291search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.0 years ago; Crawled: last week; This article first appeared in City & Country, The Edge Malaysia Weekly on October 7, 2019 - October 13, 2019Mah Sing Group Bhd launched its latest residential development, the RM500 million M Oscar, on Saturday. ... The 708 to 1,198 sq ft units, the latter of which are dual-key, offer 2 to 4-bedroom layouts and are going for RM428,000 onwards.\n\nThis article first appeared in City & Country, The Edge Malaysia Weekly on October 7, 2019 - October 13, 2019\n\nMah Sing Group Bhd launched its latest residential development, the RM500 million M Oscar, on Saturday.\n\nLocated on a 4.63-acre freehold parcel off Kuchai Lama in Kuala Lumpur, the project comprises two blocks of serviced apartments with 910 units in total and is scheduled for completion in September 2023.\n\nThe 708 to 1,198 sq ft units, the latter of which are dual-key, offer 2 to 4-bedroom layouts and are going for RM428,000 onwards.\n\n“The name and concept of M Oscar are interpretations of the aspirations of urban dwellers who work hard to achieve their dreams and are rewarded with a place they can call home,” said Mah Sing Group director of strategy and operations Lionel Leong at the opening of M Oscar’s sales gallery last Wednesday.\n\nThe guest of honour at the event was the Prime Minister’s Special Envoy to China Tan Kok Wai. Also present were Mah Sing founder and group managing director Tan Sri Leong Hoy Kum and CEO Datuk Ho Han Sang.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nM Oscar | M GROUP (https://www.mahsing-realstate.com/projects/kuchai-lama-condo-m-oscar)\nciteturn291search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; M Oscar offers a range of practical layouts (700 – 708 sq.ft), designed for couples, families and investors alike.\n\nM M Oscar RESIDENCES\n\n# M Oscar\n\nFreehold Residence KL Sold Out\n\nType\n\nFreehold Residence\n\nTenure\n\nFreehold\n\nBuilt-up\n\n700 – 708 sq.ft\n\nStatus\n\nSold Out\n\nIntroduction\n\n## A Jewel Amongst the Stars.\n\nSearching for a condo near Kuchai Lama to call your dream home? Then the M Oscar condominium might just be the one that captures your heart with its beautiful design and astounding features!\n\nBe blown away by the breathtaking landscapes and designs of the M Oscar, a new project in Kuchai Lama. The beautiful landscaping on its facilities and play areas incorporates an urban rendition with a touch of nature, reminiscent of serene wetlands and meandering streams.\n\nAlso inspired by nature's rugged canyons carved over the millennia, the exquisite design of this upcoming new condo's lobby entrance will not fail to greet you with grandeur upon each arrival.\n\nThe M Oscar condominium stands tall and bedazzling at 100m above sea level in Kuchai Lama, making it a jewel amongst the stars. This allows you to relish in the romantic night-time atmosphere and marvel at the stars that decorate the sky above as well as below through the windows of your sanctuary.\n\nThe M Oscar is an upcoming freehold residence condominium in Kuchai Lama with units that are built with a North-South orientation. Each unit also comes with 2 to 4 car parks, making it suitable for couples and families.\n\nOne of the key features of this new condo is the 2.7-acre podium deck, which is an ideal spot for friends and family to relax whilst basking in its beautiful surroundings. This one-of-a-kind podium deck is meticulously designed with community and wholesome living in mind and consists of 12 zones with a total of 35 types of facilities to cater to residents of this condo in Kuchai Lama.\n\n  * Strategic connectivity to major highways\n  * Integrated lifestyle amenities & facilities\n  * Sustainable, community-first master plan\n  * Smart-home ready & energy efficient\n\nFeatures\n\n## Facilities & Amenities\n\nMulti-tier security\n\nEV charging stations\n\nDelivery parcel lockers\n\nInfinity pool & sky lounge\n\nLandscaped gardens\n\nExcellent highway & transit access\n\nLayouts\n\n## Unit Types\n\nType A\n\n2 Bedrooms · 2 Baths\n\nBuilt-up: 700 – 708 sq.ft\n\nType B\n\n3 Bedrooms · 2 Baths\n\nBuilt-up: 700 – 708 sq.ft\n\nType C\n\n4 Bedrooms · 2 Baths\n\nBuilt-up: 708 sq.ft\n\nLocation\n\n## Connectivity & Amenities\n\n  * Major highway access near KL\n  * MRT / LRT / KTM stations within reach\n  * Shopping malls, schools & medical centres nearby\n  * Parks and everyday retail conveniences\n\n### Sales Gallery\n\nM Oscar Sales Gallery, KL\n\nMap of M Oscar\n\nFAQ\n\n## About M Oscar\n\nWhat unit types are available at M Oscar?+\n\nM Oscar offers a range of practical layouts (700 – 708 sq.ft), designed for couples, families and investors alike.\n\nIs M Oscar freehold or leasehold?+\n\nM Oscar is a freehold development in KL.\n\nWhat is the pricing for M Oscar?+\n\nM Oscar is fully sold. Register your interest to be notified of resale or upcoming phases.----------------------------------------------------------------------